From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shlomi Marco <s.marco@rubycomm.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: phy: rockchip-inno-usb2: fix OTG state machine race and timer
 cleanup

Fix two related issues with the OTG state machine delayed works:

1. During probe, extcon_set_state_sync() fires the rockchip_otg_event
   notifier which schedules otg_sm_work with a 2-second delay. When
   this fires, DWC3 has already called phy_power_on() (suspended=false),
   but the state machine sees state=UNDEFINED with no VBUS and calls
   phy_power_off(), killing the 480MHz clock and dropping USB from
   high-speed (480Mbps) to full-speed (12Mbps).

   Fix by using extcon_set_state() instead of extcon_set_state_sync()
   for the initial state sync during probe. This sets the cable state
   for DWC3 to read via extcon_get_state() without firing notifiers
   that schedule the premature work.

2. The OTG state machine delayed works (otg_sm_work, chg_work, sm_work)
   are not canceled when the device is removed or when probe fails.
   This causes a use-after-free because the scheduled work fires after
   the driver data has been freed.

   Fix by registering devm cleanup actions that cancel all pending
   delayed works when the device is removed or probe unwinds.

Signed-off-by: Shlomi Marco <s.marco@rubycomm.com>
---
 drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c | 33 ++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
@@ -1358,7 +1358,15 @@ static int rockchip_usb2phy_otg_port_init(struct rockchip_usb2phy *rphy,
 		if (!of_property_present(rphy->dev->of_node, "extcon")) {
-			/* do initial sync of usb state */
+			/*
+			 * Set initial USB host state without firing
+			 * notifiers. Using extcon_set_state_sync() here
+			 * would trigger rockchip_otg_event() which
+			 * schedules the OTG state machine work before
+			 * the PHY consumer (e.g. DWC3) has called
+			 * phy_init()/phy_power_on(), causing a premature
+			 * phy_power_off() that drops USB to full-speed.
+			 */
 			id = property_enabled(rphy->grf, &rport->port_cfg->utmi_id);
-			extcon_set_state_sync(rphy->edev, EXTCON_USB_HOST, !id);
+			extcon_set_state(rphy->edev, EXTCON_USB_HOST, !id);
 		}
 	}
 
@@ -1367,6 +1374,21 @@ out:
 	return ret;
 }
 
+static void rockchip_usb2phy_otg_work_cleanup(void *data)
+{
+	struct rockchip_usb2phy_port *rport = data;
+
+	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&rport->otg_sm_work);
+	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&rport->chg_work);
+}
+
+static void rockchip_usb2phy_host_work_cleanup(void *data)
+{
+	struct rockchip_usb2phy_port *rport = data;
+
+	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&rport->sm_work);
+}
+
 static int rockchip_usb2phy_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
@@ -1496,7 +1518,14 @@ static int rockchip_usb2phy_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 			if (ret)
 				goto put_child;
 		}
-
+		ret = devm_add_action_or_reset(dev,
+			of_node_name_eq(child_np, "host-port") ?
+				rockchip_usb2phy_host_work_cleanup :
+				rockchip_usb2phy_otg_work_cleanup,
+			rport);
+		if (ret)
+			goto put_child;
+
 next_child:
 		/* to prevent out of boundary */
 		if (++index >= rphy->phy_cfg->num_ports)
--
Armbian
